01:37:23.160 --> 01:37:25.340
with direction, with fulfillment.

2582
01:37:25.340 --> 01:37:27.160
And it doesn't mean that you have to quit your job

2583
01:37:27.160 --> 01:37:30.170
or that this even needs to be your primary focus,

2584
01:37:30.170 --> 01:37:33.460
but devoting some part of your energy

2585
01:37:33.460 --> 01:37:38.370
or your intention to that, first through therapy

2586
01:37:38.370 --> 01:37:40.730
or some kind of modality to help you cope

2587
01:37:40.730 --> 01:37:42.800
and process what has happened to you,

2588
01:37:42.800 --> 01:37:44.290
which is an act of self love.

2589
01:37:44.290 --> 01:37:47.010
And then after that, through service,

2590
01:37:47.010 --> 01:37:50.103
which is an act of love for other people.

2591
01:37:51.100 --> 01:37:52.250
That was so beautiful Rich,

2592
01:37:52.250 --> 01:37:55.280
I can't add anything to that other than just say

2593
01:37:55.280 --> 01:37:57.620
you're a primary care physician as well.

2594
01:37:57.620 --> 01:38:02.620
So you're already living a very cool life of like,

2595
01:38:02.620 --> 01:38:05.920
you're kind of leaning towards service already.

2596
01:38:05.920 --> 01:38:10.330
You know, I think it's when you have a broken heart,

2597
01:38:10.330 --> 01:38:13.500
you feel, I think you can feel more

2598
01:38:13.500 --> 01:38:15.440
what people have gone through.

2599
01:38:15.440 --> 01:38:17.770
I think it allows you to be more empathetic

2600
01:38:18.930 --> 01:38:21.130
and I think that there's power in that

2601
01:38:21.130 --> 01:38:23.850
and not power like personal power,

2602
01:38:23.850 --> 01:38:27.730
but power in your ability to reach others

2603
01:38:27.730 --> 01:38:29.180
and to reach parts of yourself,

2604
01:38:29.180 --> 01:38:31.100
maybe that you didn't even know were there.

2605
01:38:31.100 --> 01:38:32.450
And I just wanna commend you

2606
01:38:32.450 --> 01:38:34.720
for living a cool life already

2607
01:38:34.720 --> 01:38:38.330
and for sharing this in this way.

2608
01:38:38.330 --> 01:38:41.410
And you know, life is a beautiful gift

2609
01:38:41.410 --> 01:38:42.750
and so we can't forget that,

2610
01:38:42.750 --> 01:38:43.940
no matter everything that happens,

2611
01:38:43.940 --> 01:38:45.750
we have to remember that life is a beautiful gift.

2612
01:38:45.750 --> 01:38:50.750
Whatever is happening out there, it's often tragic,

2613
01:38:51.990 --> 01:38:53.330
but it is a gift.

2614
01:38:53.330 --> 01:38:57.410
So we have to remember.

2615
01:38:57.410 --> 01:39:01.310
Yeah a hundred percent man, a hundred percent.

2616
01:39:01.310 --> 01:39:03.670
Well, good I think that's a good place to put a pin in it.

2617
01:39:03.670 --> 01:39:05.710
We're gonna turn our attention to

2618
01:39:06.550 --> 01:39:09.500
coaching call with Chris, but Adam, thank you.

2619
01:39:09.500 --> 01:39:10.333
Thank you.

2620
01:39:10.333 --> 01:39:11.166
Appreciate you.

2621
01:39:11.166 --> 01:39:12.460
Appreciate you.

2622
01:39:12.460 --> 01:39:14.750
I love you and I'll see you back here in two weeks.

2623
01:39:14.750 --> 01:39:16.340
I love you too, where's my Rollies.

2624
01:39:16.340 --> 01:39:17.820
Let's go party.

2625
01:39:17.820 --> 01:39:21.080
We gotta decide maybe we should outsource the,

2626
01:39:21.080 --> 01:39:24.650
or just you know, just put it out to the audience

2627
01:39:24.650 --> 01:39:27.210
to come up with designs for the Rollie trophy.

2628
01:39:27.210 --> 01:39:28.435
Yeah.

2629
01:39:28.435 --> 01:39:29.558
And see what we get.

2630
01:39:29.558 --> 01:39:30.391
I think that's a good idea.

2631
01:39:30.391 --> 01:39:32.440
I'm gonna go celebrate with fellow Rollie winner,

2632
01:39:32.440 --> 01:39:33.999
Jason Camiolo.

2633
01:39:33.999 --> 01:39:35.820
Yeah at the after party.

2634
01:39:35.820 --> 01:39:37.659
Where's the after party?

2635
01:39:37.659 --> 01:39:40.640
(both chuckle)

2636
01:39:40.640 --> 01:39:42.380
Yes behind the velvet row.

2637
01:39:42.380 --> 01:39:43.490
Yes, yes, of course.

2638
01:39:43.490 --> 01:39:44.660
Very exclusive and elite.

2639
01:39:44.660 --> 01:39:46.880
If he lost, he might've slapped us.

2640
01:39:46.880 --> 01:39:48.440
It would've been rough.

2641
01:39:48.440 --> 01:39:50.866
I'm so glad that the audience came through.

2642
01:39:50.866 --> 01:39:52.150
(chuckles) I'm glad too.

2643
01:39:52.150 --> 01:39:53.753
All right dude, see you back here in two weeks.

2644
01:39:53.753 --> 01:39:54.860
Like I said, I love you.

2645
01:39:54.860 --> 01:39:57.440
Thank you everybody for taking this journey with me

2646
01:39:57.440 --> 01:40:01.080
and "Roll On" we'll be back in two--

2647
01:40:01.080 --> 01:40:02.330
Two weeks?

2648
01:40:02.330 --> 01:40:03.358
Two weeks from now.

2649
01:40:03.358 --> 01:40:04.191
Yeah.

2650
01:40:04.191 --> 01:40:05.024
Yeah, right peace out.

2651
01:40:05.024 --> 01:40:08.830
But I guess the first thing I would ask you is, you know,

2652
01:40:08.830 --> 01:40:11.230
what is the typical experience with the athletes

2653
01:40:11.230 --> 01:40:12.530
that you're working with?

2654
01:40:12.530 --> 01:40:14.200
'Cause I'm sure a lot of them,

2655
01:40:14.200 --> 01:40:16.830
if not most of them have had COVID at some point,

2656
01:40:16.830 --> 01:40:21.220
so you have some data points on what's working,

2657
01:40:21.220 --> 01:40:23.830
what's not working, people who try to get back

2658
01:40:23.830 --> 01:40:26.131
into it too quickly, et cetera.

2659
01:40:26.131 --> 01:40:27.643
(chuckles) Yeah, I mean, that's the thing.

2660
01:40:27.643 --> 01:40:30.553
I think it's gone through every one of my athletes,

2661
01:40:30.553 --> 01:40:33.360
I can't really think of anybody who hasn't

2662
01:40:33.360 --> 01:40:34.730
besides myself (chuckles)

2663
01:40:34.730 --> 01:40:36.246
That's the crazy--

2664
01:40:36.246 --> 01:40:37.580
You still haven't had it, wow.

2665
01:40:37.580 --> 01:40:40.090
Not with four kids, that's even more surprising.

2666
01:40:40.090 --> 01:40:41.460
Right.

2667
01:40:41.460 --> 01:40:44.900
So and we have to test also going to different households

2668
01:40:44.900 --> 01:40:46.550
'cause it affects different households.

2669
01:40:46.550 --> 01:40:48.090
So if somebody's feeling under the weather

2670
01:40:48.090 --> 01:40:48.923
or something like that.

2671
01:40:48.923 --> 01:40:50.770
So anyway, but that being said,

2672
01:40:50.770 --> 01:40:52.380
your question is a legitimate one

2673
01:40:52.380 --> 01:40:56.210
because it's across the board different for every athlete.

2674
01:40:56.210 --> 01:40:59.250
But what I've found is really two camps

2675
01:40:59.250 --> 01:41:01.580
one and this is the larger group.

2676
01:41:01.580 --> 01:41:05.910
It takes longer than they thought to kick out of it.

2677
01:41:05.910 --> 01:41:09.080
They have this general sense of malaise

2678
01:41:09.080 --> 01:41:11.460
of just not being a hundred percent,

2679
01:41:11.460 --> 01:41:13.560
they feel good enough to train,

2680
01:41:13.560 --> 01:41:16.990
they feel good enough to do all the activities,

2681
01:41:16.990 --> 01:41:19.470
but they're just missing a gear or two

2682
01:41:19.470 --> 01:41:22.850
and they're surprised how long it takes.

2683
01:41:22.850 --> 01:41:25.150
And then from one day to the next,

2684
01:41:25.150 --> 01:41:29.293
the cloud lifts and they feel mostly back to normal.

2685
01:41:30.211 --> 01:41:31.300
And so they and those--

2686
01:41:31.300 --> 01:41:32.460
And in those cases, yeah in those cases

2687
01:41:32.460 --> 01:41:35.090
are you just asking people to train through it

2688
01:41:35.090 --> 01:41:36.820
and deal with it or is it better

2689
01:41:36.820 --> 01:41:41.820
to just take your foot off the gas completely or slightly?

2690
01:41:41.940 --> 01:41:44.830
Well, I think the first component there is

2691
01:41:44.830 --> 01:41:48.110
you can train or I let them train how they want to,

2692
01:41:48.110 --> 01:41:51.430
but recognize that they might not be at a hundred percent

2693
01:41:51.430 --> 01:41:55.070
and not be so hard on themselves because of it, right.

2694
01:41:55.070 --> 01:41:58.440
We're constantly evaluating how we're progressing.

2695
01:41:58.440 --> 01:42:00.023
And so it becomes this like,

2696
01:42:00.023 --> 01:42:02.270
ugh, I'm not progressing where I feel off

2697
01:42:02.270 --> 01:42:03.580
or I'm tired or I'm flat

2698
01:42:03.580 --> 01:42:05.440
or I didn't eat enough or something.

2699
01:42:05.440 --> 01:42:06.380
And I say, you know,

2700
01:42:06.380 --> 01:42:09.100
it might still just be this carrying on

2701
01:42:09.100 --> 01:42:11.110
for a longer period of time than you think.

2702
01:42:11.110 --> 01:42:14.900
So allow yourself to not necessarily once again,

2703
01:42:14.900 --> 01:42:16.520
train without intention,

2704
01:42:16.520 --> 01:42:19.480
but give yourself that little extra space

2705
01:42:19.480 --> 01:42:21.713
of forgiveness quite honestly.

2706
01:42:22.690 --> 01:42:25.750
But you don't think that the training itself

2707
01:42:25.750 --> 01:42:30.503
is ill advised or prolonging that recovery period.

2708
01:42:31.800 --> 01:42:33.670
I haven't seen it

2709
01:42:33.670 --> 01:42:36.750
because those have given more time off to,

2710
01:42:36.750 --> 01:42:40.040
or I've backed off the training completely

2711
01:42:40.040 --> 01:42:43.520
they're not necessarily getting healthier, quicker.

2712
01:42:43.520 --> 01:42:44.610
Interesting.

2713
01:42:44.610 --> 01:42:47.910
And so there's those who three, four days later

2714
01:42:47.910 --> 01:42:50.610
are basically back to normal and then maybe

2715
01:42:50.610 --> 01:42:53.690
another two, three days and then they're a hundred percent,

2716
01:42:53.690 --> 01:42:57.320
but then there's others three, four weeks

2717
01:42:57.320 --> 01:43:01.440
of just feeling just enough to notice that they're off,

2718
01:43:01.440 --> 01:43:04.560
that they just can't perform, let's say intervals

2719
01:43:04.560 --> 01:43:07.950
or strength work or paces that they were

2720
01:43:07.950 --> 01:43:09.960
before getting COVID.

2721
01:43:09.960 --> 01:43:14.960
And so it's just a close watching process for the athlete

2722
01:43:15.110 --> 01:43:18.090
and really providing the insight to me so that I can say,

2723
01:43:18.090 --> 01:43:19.220
all right, you know what?

2724
01:43:19.220 --> 01:43:21.920
We'll take out a few of these higher quality,

2725
01:43:21.920 --> 01:43:24.880
higher intensity workouts and just stay true

2726
01:43:24.880 --> 01:43:28.190
to the endurance or stay true to clean motions

2727
01:43:28.190 --> 01:43:29.410
or just good strength work.

2728
01:43:29.410 --> 01:43:31.720
Maybe we're not looking to top out the strength work,

2729
01:43:31.720 --> 01:43:36.410
but just staying connected to so that once you are healthy,

2730
01:43:36.410 --> 01:43:38.640
that you're ready to really hit that gear.

2731
01:43:38.640 --> 01:43:39.873
And that's the fun, right?

2732
01:43:39.873 --> 01:43:43.240
That you, as the athlete feel good about like, okay,

2733
01:43:43.240 --> 01:43:46.710
as soon as that fog lifts at least I'm ready

2734
01:43:46.710 --> 01:43:49.870
and I can have some really good training days.

2735
01:43:49.870 --> 01:43:53.730
Well, I feel pretty fortunate in that at least so far,

2736
01:43:53.730 --> 01:43:58.013
I don't feel that malaise or that general fatigue.

2737
01:43:59.160 --> 01:44:02.050
I thought like I might have to take a couple weeks off.

2738
01:44:02.050 --> 01:44:05.320
Like I had athletes pinging me, friends of mine,

2739
01:44:05.320 --> 01:44:06.620
and I know, you know,

2740
01:44:06.620 --> 01:44:07.970
because I know them and they're friends.

2741
01:44:07.970 --> 01:44:09.080
I know that they, you know,

2742
01:44:09.080 --> 01:44:10.860
they're not afraid to train hard.

2743
01:44:10.860 --> 01:44:12.120
Yeah.

2744
01:44:12.120 --> 01:44:13.430
And a couple of 'em were like, I took three weeks off,

2745
01:44:13.430 --> 01:44:14.400
like I just needed that.

2746
01:44:14.400 --> 01:44:17.620
But I felt pretty good pretty quickly,

2747
01:44:17.620 --> 01:44:21.330
like after four days I felt pretty much fine.

2748
01:44:21.330 --> 01:44:23.440
I was like, yeah, but I'm gonna be conservative,

2749
01:44:23.440 --> 01:44:24.777
I'm gonna sit this out.

2750
01:44:24.777 --> 01:44:26.730
And I think I took seven days off total,

2751
01:44:26.730 --> 01:44:30.860
but I felt ready to go and just very gradually

2752
01:44:30.860 --> 01:44:33.730
and gently got back into the pool, I didn't push anything.

2753
01:44:33.730 --> 01:44:36.210
Like I would go three or 4,000 yards,

2754
01:44:36.210 --> 01:44:38.440
but I didn't really do anything very hard

2755
01:44:38.440 --> 01:44:41.140
just to gauge it and see how I felt.

2756
01:44:41.140 --> 01:44:44.650
But today you gave me a 4,700 yard workout

2757
01:44:44.650 --> 01:44:47.200
and there was some hard efforts in there

2758
01:44:47.200 --> 01:44:48.520
and I felt pretty good, you know,

2759
01:44:48.520 --> 01:44:50.410
and I got through it and that's the most yardage

2760
01:44:50.410 --> 01:44:51.243
that I've done.

2761
01:44:51.243 --> 01:44:52.970
And I know there's a lot of a volume waiting for me,

2762
01:44:52.970 --> 01:44:57.640
but I'm feeling pretty grateful that I'm not in that camp

2763
01:44:57.640 --> 01:45:00.140
of feeling like I'm missing a step, maybe that'll change.

2764
01:45:00.140 --> 01:45:03.110
But right now that's kind of where I'm at.

2765
01:45:03.110 --> 01:45:07.090
But I did miss seven days on a pretty short time window,

2766
01:45:07.090 --> 01:45:09.970
I'm now eight weeks out of this swim.

2767
01:45:09.970 --> 01:45:11.900
So there's a lot of work that has to happen

2768
01:45:11.900 --> 01:45:13.230
and obviously, you know,

2769
01:45:13.230 --> 01:45:15.110
not everything has gone perfectly to plan

2770
01:45:15.110 --> 01:45:18.810
and I've got a lot more hiccups, you know, along the way,

2771
01:45:18.810 --> 01:45:20.450
over the course of the next eight weeks,

2772
01:45:20.450 --> 01:45:23.350
including this weekend where I'm gonna be driving up north

2773
01:45:24.380 --> 01:45:27.430
to your neck of the woods for an appointment for my back.

2774
01:45:27.430 --> 01:45:30.080
And I'm gonna miss a couple swim days in there as well,

2775
01:45:30.080 --> 01:45:32.810
'cause I'm doing the road trip with my kid

2776
01:45:32.810 --> 01:45:35.360
and I don't wanna be just training all the time.

2777
01:45:35.360 --> 01:45:36.193
Yeah, yeah.

2778
01:45:36.193 --> 01:45:37.680
Well, you know, there's pools up here too,

2779
01:45:37.680 --> 01:45:38.680
I could help you find it.

2780
01:45:38.680 --> 01:45:40.497
I know, that's true.

2781
01:45:40.497 --> 01:45:42.180
But like, I don't know, I'm like,

2782
01:45:42.180 --> 01:45:45.343
hey, hey Jaiya go sit in the corner while I go train.

2783
01:45:45.343 --> 01:45:47.110
Like I gotta balance that, you know,

2784
01:45:47.110 --> 01:45:51.563
it's supposed to be kind of like a father son road trip.

2785
01:45:52.407 --> 01:45:54.138
Yeah.

2786
01:45:54.138 --> 01:45:57.970
So with that being said, it's hard to know where you're at

2787
01:45:57.970 --> 01:46:00.340
with regards to the health,

2788
01:46:00.340 --> 01:46:02.580
because you might have felt pretty good today

2789
01:46:02.580 --> 01:46:04.790
because you also had a week lighter

2790
01:46:04.790 --> 01:46:07.490
leading up to it to really absorb the training

2791
01:46:07.490 --> 01:46:10.760
that you were doing prior and also increasing

2792
01:46:10.760 --> 01:46:12.400
sort of the build as you were going.

2793
01:46:12.400 --> 01:46:15.790
So it's hard to know that until we're a couple days

2794
01:46:15.790 --> 01:46:17.590
further down the road here,

2795
01:46:17.590 --> 01:46:19.530
at which point you're taking a couple days off.

2796
01:46:19.530 --> 01:46:21.460
So that's why we're taking the windows

2797
01:46:21.460 --> 01:46:24.340
and you're just a classic example of most,

2798
01:46:24.340 --> 01:46:26.910
any athlete that has a full-time (indistinct chatter)

2799
01:46:26.910 --> 01:46:28.190
as a family.

2800
01:46:28.190 --> 01:46:30.210
Like it's stressful for all of us.

2801
01:46:30.210 --> 01:46:31.500
And that's the whole challenge,

2802
01:46:31.500 --> 01:46:35.430
how to navigate these little windows when we can train

2803
01:46:35.430 --> 01:46:39.440
and using the time we have to maximize the fitness gains.

2804
01:46:39.440 --> 01:46:44.440
And so here we are eight weeks out to do 21,000 yards

2805
01:46:44.940 --> 01:46:47.570
in one fell swoop.

2806
01:46:47.570 --> 01:46:49.910
Right, so what am I looking at here?

2807
01:46:49.910 --> 01:46:53.480
How you know, is this volume gonna escalate?

2808
01:46:53.480 --> 01:46:55.680
Cause I'm itching, I'm always itching

2809
01:46:55.680 --> 01:46:57.380
at this phase to be doing more.

2810
01:46:57.380 --> 01:47:00.620
And you're always like pushing me to slow down a little bit,

2811
01:47:00.620 --> 01:47:02.450
but I've worked with you long enough to know

2812
01:47:02.450 --> 01:47:04.600
like those days are coming.

2813
01:47:04.600 --> 01:47:06.670
Yeah, well the beauty is we're starting

2814
01:47:06.670 --> 01:47:09.790
that sort of the bigger prep this week

2815
01:47:09.790 --> 01:47:11.430
with some longer sets,

2816
01:47:11.430 --> 01:47:14.470
I'm hopeful that we can get in two key workouts this week

2817
01:47:14.470 --> 01:47:17.290
and they include some long continuous swimming

2818
01:47:17.290 --> 01:47:19.430
and you're gonna curse me plenty then,

2819
01:47:19.430 --> 01:47:21.480
when you say I wanna do more,

2820
01:47:21.480 --> 01:47:24.520
and then I have two 1800 straight for you waiting

2821
01:47:24.520 --> 01:47:25.893
with four minutes rest.

2822
01:47:26.921 --> 01:47:27.820
(chuckles) And you're gonna do that in the pool

2823
01:47:27.820 --> 01:47:31.210
and be like really this my brain is going mush

2824
01:47:31.210 --> 01:47:32.920
back to our youth.

2825
01:47:32.920 --> 01:47:33.840
No, I love that stuff.

2826
01:47:33.840 --> 01:47:36.150
But the good thing is that with that, you know,

2827
01:47:36.150 --> 01:47:38.770
with our watches these days, we no longer have to count.

2828
01:47:38.770 --> 01:47:42.100
Remember back in the day, if we had to swim longer,

2829
01:47:42.100 --> 01:47:44.780
we didn't know if we missed the 50 or 100

2830
01:47:44.780 --> 01:47:45.613
or something.

2831
01:47:45.613 --> 01:47:48.720
Now we can just look at our watch, so lucky on that.

2832
01:47:48.720 --> 01:47:49.553
But that being said,

2833
01:47:49.553 --> 01:47:53.860
it's a great opportunity to swim 3,600 yards broken

2834
01:47:53.860 --> 01:47:57.110
